* Detection: Denied access attempts against private key material
*
* Hypothesis:
*   Denied reads against private keys are a direct indicator of credential
*   theft attempts. Unlike most signals, this one has very little benign
*   explanation — a process that should read a key normally has permission
*   to do so.
*
* Matches on denial plus key-related terms rather than a fixed path, since
* key material is not always stored where policy says it should be.
*
* Tuning notes:
*   - The system generates some of these in normal background operation.
*     Baseline those before alerting.
*   - A denial from an unexpected user or process context is the high-value
*     case. Denials from known service accounts are usually noise.
*   - Successful reads by unexpected principals are worse than denials and
*     will not appear in this query. A companion query should cover those.

index="splunk_data" "denied" AND ("key" OR "private" OR ".pem")
| table _time, host, _raw
